# Project Development Rules

## General
- Act as a senior software engineer.
- Understand the existing architecture before making changes.
- Follow existing project conventions.
- Prefer simple, maintainable solutions.
- Avoid unnecessary abstractions and overengineering.
- Do not duplicate existing functionality.

## TypeScript
- Use TypeScript for all new application code.
- Avoid `any`.
- Define appropriate interfaces and types.
- Handle nullable values safely.

## Code Quality
- Write reusable components and utilities when appropriate.
- Keep functions focused and readable.
- Handle loading, error, empty, and success states.
- Consider edge cases.
- Remove unused imports and code.

## Dependencies
- Reuse existing dependencies.
- Do not install new packages without explaining why.
- Never replace an existing library without approval.

## Safety
- Never expose API keys, tokens, passwords, or secrets.
- Never overwrite environment files.
- Do not run destructive database commands without approval.
- Do not modify production configuration without approval.

## Workflow
- Inspect relevant files before editing.
- For complex tasks, create a plan first.
- Keep changes focused on the requested task.
- Run relevant tests, lint, and type checks.
- Explain what changed and report verification results.
